WEBVTT

legitimacy-05-1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:06.460
Previously: five forces loosened this
production line, section by section.

legitimacy-05-2
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:12.800
This time: someone steps onto the stage
with a toolbox, hoping to repair it.

legitimacy-05-3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.290
Episode 5: Beyond Repair

legitimacy-05-4
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.911
When the line comes loose, someone always
wants to fix it. The thesis identifies

legitimacy-05-5
00:00:24.911 --> 00:00:26.370
two common kinds of repair.

legitimacy-05-6
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:32.325
One is nostalgic restoration: stick the
old symbols back on. The other is radical

legitimacy-05-7
00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:35.560
re-identification: simply create a new
“we.”

legitimacy-05-8
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.218
Author's thesis §3.3.4: symbolic efforts
to repair a legitimacy crisis often take

legitimacy-05-9
00:00:38.218 --> 00:00:40.680
two forms—nostalgic restoration and
radical re-identification. (Paraphrase)

legitimacy-05-10
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:47.650
Repairer one covers every crack with
nostalgic stickers: flags, anthems,

legitimacy-05-11
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:52.950
myths, time-honored brands. Suddenly the
whole line looks lively.

legitimacy-05-12
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:58.510
But the screws are still loose. Stickers
can offer comfort, but not coherence.

legitimacy-05-13
00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:01.829
Author's thesis §3.3.4: restoration fails
because it cannot address the structural

legitimacy-05-14
00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:04.500
conditions of symbolic rupture—“it offers
comfort, not coherence.”

legitimacy-05-15
00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:11.650
Repairer two does not fix the old
machine. She wants to create a new “we,”

legitimacy-05-16
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.090
with a purity test posted at the
entrance.

legitimacy-05-17
00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:20.090
She meant to escape the old logic of
exclusion, but ends up drawing another

legitimacy-05-18
00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.090
line: “us” on this side, “them” on the
other.

legitimacy-05-19
00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.215
Author's thesis §3.3.4: radical
re-identification often reproduces the

legitimacy-05-20
00:01:25.215 --> 00:01:27.462
logic of exclusion and classification it
seeks to escape. Even in dissent,

legitimacy-05-21
00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:29.770
symbolic grammar remains trapped in the
old logic of “us/them.” (Paraphrase)

legitimacy-05-22
00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:36.895
Why can neither repair it? Return first
to the foundation of modern legitimacy: a

legitimacy-05-23
00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:38.680
space of representation.

legitimacy-05-24
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.724
The state is the machine; the nation is
its justification; sovereignty welds them

legitimacy-05-25
00:01:42.724 --> 00:01:45.420
together. The picture inside the frame is
called “us.”

legitimacy-05-26
00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.507
Author's thesis §3.4: modern political
legitimacy depends on Lefort's (1986)

legitimacy-05-27
00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.595
“space of representation.” The state is
the material apparatus of power, the

legitimacy-05-28
00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:51.517
nation its cultural-symbolic
justification, and sovereignty where they

legitimacy-05-29
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:53.330
fuse through claims to legitimacy (the
thesis cites Walker, 1993).

legitimacy-05-30
00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:01.179
But in postmodernity, the picture inside
the frame is gone. Signs no longer point

legitimacy-05-31
00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:05.120
to anything outside the frame; they point
only to one another.

legitimacy-05-32
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.655
Stickers go on top of stickers; the new
doorway draws its line in relation to the

legitimacy-05-33
00:02:09.655 --> 00:02:13.630
old one. Both repairers are restoring a
picture no longer in the frame.

legitimacy-05-34
00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:16.070
Author's thesis §3.4: as Baudrillard
(1994) argues, late-modern representation

legitimacy-05-35
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.479
no longer reflects reality but replaces
it. Signs no longer refer to external

legitimacy-05-36
00:02:18.479 --> 00:02:20.200
meaning, but circulate
self-referentially. (Paraphrase)

legitimacy-05-37
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.502
Distinguish two things: the state as an
administrative and security machine can

legitimacy-05-38
00:02:27.502 --> 00:02:28.490
keep running.

legitimacy-05-39
00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:34.290
What collapses is the nation as the
reason “why we are together.”

legitimacy-05-40
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.175
Author's thesis §3.4: “while the nation
as an administrative or security

legitimacy-05-41
00:02:37.175 --> 00:02:40.260
apparatus may survive, the nation as an
ontological justification collapses.”

legitimacy-05-42
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:48.050
Vote: which repair seems more common to
you? A: nostalgic stickers; B: a doorway

legitimacy-05-43
00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.620
with a purity test. Tell us in the
comments.

legitimacy-05-44
00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.117
A caveat: repairs fail not because the
repairers are foolish, but because the

legitimacy-05-45
00:02:56.117 --> 00:02:58.920
thing they are trying to repair is
already gone.

legitimacy-05-46
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.600
This does not mock nostalgia or
resistance. The longing is real, and so

legitimacy-05-47
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:10.360
are the wounds. The problem is that both
repairs use the old blueprints.

legitimacy-05-48
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.300
This episode's reference card (take a
screenshot)

legitimacy-05-49
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.733
Nostalgic restoration | Nostalgic
stickers over cracks | Offers comfort,

legitimacy-05-50
00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:18.400
not coherence.

legitimacy-05-51
00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.551
Radical re-identification | A new doorway
with a purity test | Draws another

legitimacy-05-52
00:03:22.551 --> 00:03:23.370
“us/them” line.

legitimacy-05-53
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.282
Space of representation | A picture frame
held up by three pillars | The state is

legitimacy-05-54
00:03:26.282 --> 00:03:27.900
the machine; the nation is the
justification.

legitimacy-05-55
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.201
Why repair fails | The picture inside the
frame is already gone | The machine

legitimacy-05-56
00:03:33.201 --> 00:03:35.610
remains; its justification is gone.

legitimacy-05-57
00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:40.760
Another sticker has been added to the
passport.

legitimacy-05-58
00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.390
Its edges are still blurred.

legitimacy-05-59
00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.050
Next episode:

legitimacy-05-60
00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.416
The audience leaves; someone brings a
little lectern of their own. Do

legitimacy-05-61
00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:56.060
dissenters resemble a small state?

legitimacy-05-62
00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:03.270
This is UjiBricks.
